cves.impact:
This vulnerability may allow remote attackers to cause a denial-of-service (DoS) on the NGINX system or to possibly trigger a code execution. There is no control plane exposure; this is a data plane issue only.

For example, the following configuration would be vulnerable because the rewrite directive is configured with a query string (?) and followed by the set directive with an unnamed capture group ($1):

location / {
    rewrite ^/old/(.*)$ /new?upgrade=1;
    set $orig $1;
}

cves.mitigation:
To mitigate this vulnerability, use named captures instead of unnamed captures in rewrite definitions.

For example, the rewrite directive in the Impact section could be rewritten as:

location / {
    rewrite ^/old/(?<orig>.*)$ /new?upgrade=1;
}

